fuel[1] = 25;
fuel[2] = 30;

Change the declaration to `int fuel[3] = {10, 20, 0};` or simply `int fuel[3];`. This allocates enough space for indices 0, 1, and 2.

```cpp
int fuel[3] = {10, 20, 0};
fuel[0] = 15;
fuel[1] = 25;
fuel[2] = 30;
```

